1
00:00:00,101 --> 00:00:02,480
You already know what they do on third and long.

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:05,787
It's in the film. It's just spread across a week of clips,

3
00:00:05,787 --> 00:00:08,060
a legal pad, and somebody's spreadsheet.

4
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:10,530
By the time it's a call sheet,

5
00:00:10,530 --> 00:00:11,580
half your week is gone.

6
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:13,920
OFFGRD pulls it into one place.

7
00:00:15,050 --> 00:00:16,330
Chart your film once.

8
00:00:17,109 --> 00:00:20,190
OFFGRD reads your breakdown the way you exported it.

9
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:22,681
No re-tagging, no converting,

10
00:00:22,681 --> 00:00:26,450
no learning somebody else's names for your own formations.

11
00:00:27,210 --> 00:00:31,310
Map your vocabulary one time and it holds everywhere after.

12
00:00:31,890 --> 00:00:34,850
Scout cards come out the other side, already built.

13
00:00:36,115 --> 00:00:38,975
Sunday morning, the scout becomes a game plan.

14
00:00:39,435 --> 00:00:42,600
Pull plays from your book or draw new ones animated,

15
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,618
in your own terminology

16
00:00:44,618 --> 00:00:47,075
and build the attack against each look they showed.

17
00:00:47,715 --> 00:00:53,734
And here's the part that changes your week: every play in the plan is testable the moment you save it.

18
00:00:54,255 --> 00:00:56,008
Assign the tests Sunday night.

19
00:00:56,008 --> 00:00:59,995
Your roster is studying the plan before Monday's practice.

20
00:01:01,126 --> 00:01:03,766
All week, the tests tell you what actually stuck.

21
00:01:04,225 --> 00:01:08,342
Reads, coverage ID, assignments graded, by player,

22
00:01:08,342 --> 00:01:10,286
by position group.

23
00:01:10,826 --> 00:01:12,602
Drill what the scores expose.

24
00:01:12,602 --> 00:01:14,445
Trim what they've mastered.

25
00:01:15,246 --> 00:01:19,225
The scout team runs their actual plays off cards nobody had to draw.

26
00:01:19,585 --> 00:01:22,725
By Thursday, who's ready isn't a feeling. It's a number.

27
00:01:23,006 --> 00:01:25,805
And Friday's grades become next Monday's focus.

28
00:01:26,894 --> 00:01:31,319
Around all of it, the Coaches Hub runs the program

29
00:01:31,319 --> 00:01:34,716
roster, depth chart, schedule, messaging one place,

30
00:01:34,716 --> 00:01:35,894
every coach.

31
00:01:36,414 --> 00:01:39,995
And the film you've been charting all season?

32
00:01:39,995 --> 00:01:42,054
That's your kids' recruiting film.

33
00:01:42,914 --> 00:01:45,249
The OFFRD recruiting stack is built in

34
00:01:45,249 --> 00:01:49,713
the same system that calls Friday night helps get your players to the next level.

35
00:01:50,992 --> 00:01:53,044
Friday night, you open O Caller.

36
00:01:53,044 --> 00:01:56,237
It already knows the down, the distance, the field zone.

37
00:01:56,237 --> 00:01:58,949
It shows you what they're likely to give you,

38
00:01:58,949 --> 00:02:01,991
and the calls from your book that have worked against that look.

39
00:02:01,991 --> 00:02:03,132
One tap grades the play.

40
00:02:03,832 --> 00:02:08,872
Your call sheet and your self-scout, done as you go.

41
00:02:09,592 --> 00:02:12,192
D Caller does the same on the other side of the ball.

42
00:02:13,423 --> 00:02:15,240
And when the press box wifi drops,

43
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:16,882
both of them keep working.

44
00:02:17,143 --> 00:02:19,062
OFFGRD. Never off guard.

